{
  "_doc": "Megaflora — the big things. The ask was 'give another pass over each biome and add large objects … giant trees, boulders, arches, or other features. They should be 2-3 times taller than our tallest trees currently.' The tallest ordinary prop in js/props.js is the conifer at 9 metres, so everything here stands between 17 and 26 — two to three times that — and every land biome gets at least one. They are rolled on their OWN random stream (see the `0x4d67` salt in props.js) so that adding them did not reshuffle a single tree that was already there.",

  "_schema": {
    "kinds": "the catalogue. `tall` is roughly how high it stands (the test checks it against the tallest ordinary tree), `solid` is [radius, height] for the collision field — carried here rather than in js/collide.js's PROP_SOLIDS because that file belongs to somebody else this round, `leafy` says the biome's leaf tint applies.",
    "biomes": "[[kind, chance per 64 m prop cell at density 1]] — a chance of 0.02 is about four in the block of ground you can see, which is rare enough that each one still reads as a place.",
    "minSlope": "steeper than this and nothing this big would have stayed up",
    "roadClear": "how much road under a point rules it out — nobody lets a 24 m tree grow through the highway"
  },

  "minSlope": 0.42,
